---
source: crates/omnifs-cli/tests/cli_transcripts.rs
expression: "fixture.transcript(&fixture.run(&[\"attachment\", \"--help\"]))"
---
exit: 0
stdout:
Add, list, inspect, remove, restart, or enter Attachments

Usage: omnifs attachment [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  add      Add a platform-supported Attachment
  ls       List desired Attachments and their observed state
  show     Show one desired Attachment and its observed state
  rm       Remove an Attachment from desired state
  restart  Restart an Attachment through a durable action
  shell    Enter the Attachment or run a command in its runtime
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

Global options:
  -v, --verbose...       Increase tracing verbosity. -v = info, -vv = debug with span events.
                         Overridden by `RUST_LOG`
      --output <OUTPUT>  Output contract for this invocation [default: human] [possible values:
                         human, json, jsonl]
  -q, --quiet            Suppress conversational narration on stderr. Receipts, progress settle
                         lines, and errors are preserved
      --no-input         Reject prompts and browser handoffs
      --yes              Approve confirmation-only decisions
stderr:
